---
description: Put each component in its own small file, and group a feature in a subfolder
alwaysApply: true
---

# One component per file

Each React component lives in its own file. A feature made of several components lives in a subfolder named after that feature. Keep every file small: one component, plus only the helpers that exist for that component. When a file holds a second component, or is too long to read in one pass, split it.

```text
# Bad — DatePicker, DateRange, and RangeDay share one file
src/shared/date-picker/date-picker.tsx

# Good — date-range pieces sit together, one component per file
src/shared/date-picker/date-picker.tsx
src/shared/date-picker/date-range/date-range.tsx
src/shared/date-picker/date-range/range-day.tsx
src/shared/date-picker/date-range/date-token.tsx
src/shared/date-picker/iso-date.ts
src/shared/date-picker/index.ts
```

Re-export the public components from the feature `index.ts`. Call sites import from that barrel, not from a file deep in the subfolder.
